2. Generation of basic VaLOR SK predictions and comparison against predictions from alternative analyses
............................................................................................................................

Test VaLOR Nsk. Generates summary tables (modes grouped) with/without BANFF tuning
root2k -l -b -q $T2KOSCANA/macros/spectra/test_nsk.C

--
Test nominal VaLOR spectra. 
Gives a mode-by-mode breakdown. Also saves spectra to files.
root2k -l -b -q $T2KOSCANA/macros/spectra/test_sk_ereco_spectrum_nominal.C

--
Compare spectra (nominal, with tuning steps) w/ KDI or VaLOR
Make spectra using the following steps:

Turn on __save_templates_debug__ in SuperkMC.cxx
Recompile
root2k -l -b -q $T2KOSCANA/macros/spectra/test_nsk.C
mv Template_mcnorm_fluxtuned_banfftuned_syst_phys.root sk_spectra_nobanff_osc.root; mv Template_mcnorm_fluxtuned.root sk_spectra_nobanff_noosc.root; mv Template_mcnorm_fluxtuned_banfftuned.root sk_spectra_banffpst_noosc.root; rm Template_*
Rememeber to turn off the debug option (it's slow!)

The root files have mode by mode:
 2D templates (nsk_nom_0_*) where * is mode index
 1D Etrue spectra (e.g. enu_int_nueb_ncoth)  names use KDI notation
 1D Ereco spectra (e.g. erec_int_nueb_ncoth) names use KDI notation. Use an old binning
 1D Ereco spectra (e.g. erec_int_nueb_ncoth_fine) names use KDI notation. Use the 73 bins in the analysis
and also:
 1D total Ereco spectrum: ereco_spectrum
Have the cases:
 No BANFF tuning, no oscillations
 No BANFF tuning, with oscillations
 BANFF tuning, no oscillations
So that we can compare BANFF tuning separately to oscillations

--
COMPARE SPECTRA TWEAKED w/ KDI or VaLOR
$T2KOSCANA/macros/spectra/test_sk_ereco_spectrum_twk_sys_runAll.py

Makes a ROOT file with lots of Ereco spectra:
 Nominal BANFF tuned: total & modes
 +-1,+-3 sigma tweaked: total & modes, and ratios to nominal

--
COMPARE ERROR BUDGET ON NSK (tweak categories of errors, many times)
$T2KOSCANA/macros/spectra/test_sk_ereco_spectrum_twk_sys_throw_runAll.py -n 20000

Makes the error on Nsk table for the categories (total, skdetfsi, BANFF, xsec)

--
CHECK ERROR EFFECT ON NSK (1 sigma tweaks on individual systematics)
root2k -l -b -q $T2KOSCANA/macros/spectra/test_systematic_error_propagation_all.C

Norm systematics can be checked against the input, using
root2k -l -b -q $T2KOSCANA/macros/spectra/test_systematic_error_propagation_expectation.C



3.     Running fit bias studies
............................................................................................................................
Do the fits using:
	$T2KOSCANA/production/submit_toyexpt_fitting_job_with_sys --resource RAL --tag bias_now --nruns 300 --nexpts 34 --fit-param-list nuosc3f_numudisapp_fix4+nuisance --job-dir $PWD --softw-dir $T2KOSCANA --cpu-time 48:00:00 --stat-fluctuations --tweak-systematics 1 --sinsq2theta23 0.9
Analysis using:
	root2k -l -b -q '$T2KOSCANA/macros/fit/pulls/mock_data_fit_pulls.C("bias_now*.root","bias_now",2,1,0,"analysis_configuration.xml",false)'



4. Running sensitivity studies
............................................................................................................................
Make toys using:
	 $T2KOSCANA/macros/fit/toymc/generate_toymc_ensemble.C
Submit chisq surface jobs using (be sensible with step size (not too small) & not too wide with min/max, or jobs will take forever):
	$T2KOSCANA/production/submit_toyexpt_fitting_job_xml --resource RAL --tag minos --nruns 1000 --nexpts 1 --first-expt 0 --fit-param-list nuosc3f_numudisapp_fix4+nuisance --job-dir $PWD --softw-dir $T2KOSCANA --toy-expts-file /path/to/xml/file --cpu-time 72:00:00 --chisqsyst-mixing23-min 0.93 --chisqsyst-mixing23-max 1.00 --chisqsyst-dm23sq-min 0.0021 --chisqsyst-dm23sq-max 0.0029 --chisqwithsyst-mixing23-step 0.01 --chisqwithsyst-dm23sq-step 1E-5
Make sensitivity
	$T2KOSCANA/macros/contour/const_dchisq/numu/sensitivity_from_many_chisq_surfaces.C
Plot a few sensitivities on the same graph
	macros/misc/toms_plotting_stuff/plot_minos_sensitivity_studies.C



